\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Weep not for Him who onward bears
\par His Cross to Calvary;
\par He does not ask man's pitying tears,
\par Who wills for man to die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The awful sorrow of His face,
\par The bowing of His frame,
\par Come not from torture nor disgrace:
\par He fears not Cross nor shame.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. There is a deeper pang or grief,
\par An agony unknown,
\par In which His love finds no relief-
\par He bears it all alone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. He sees the souls for whom He dies
\par Yet clinging to their sin,
\par And heirs of mansions in the skies
\par Who will not enter in.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O may I in Thy sorrow share,
\par And mourn that sins of mine
\par Should ever wound with grief or care
\par That loving heart of Thine.
\par                                     Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

